== Trivia ==
* Using the console command "<code>restart 40</code>" starts a new run as only Tainted Soul; he's still unable to fire and otherwise acts identically to {{c|The Lost}}, dying in one hit. It's not normally possible to play the game this way, and the game will crash if Tainted Soul dies while not linked to Tainted Forgotten.
* Tainted Soul bears resemblance to a scrapped character from ''Antibirth'' named [[anti:Edith|Edith]]. The mechanic used by Tainted Forgotten also resembles one planned mechanic Edith was going to have.
** It was confirmed by both Kilburn<ref>https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/485133685881045014/835354592409681970/unknown.png</ref> and Edmund McMillen<ref>https://twitter.com/edmundmcmillen/status/1389477631716958208</ref> that Edith ultimately evolved into Tainted Forgotten during development.
* Certain transformations such as {{tf|Guppy}} cause Tainted Forgotten to have the transformation's body sprite, making him stand up-right.
* The achievement for unlocking Tainted Forgotten is "The Fettered", a possible title for the character.
** "Fettered" means "bound" or "shackled", which may be linked to how Tainted Forgotten cannot move on his own and only through Tainted Soul.
** "Fettered" can also mean "restrained with chains", in a complete irony that while Tainted Forgotten and Tainted Soul are no longer physically connected to each other by chains, they are unable to progress the basement without each other, making them metaphorically chained to each other.
** According to the Binding of Isaac card game: four souls, the Tainted Soul Is labeled As “The Fettered” while Tainted Forgotten Alone is the Dead Weight.
* The character's main mechanic of picking up and carrying around a pile of bones could be a reference to [https://biblehub.com/bsb/exodus/13.htm Exodus 13:19], in which Moses carries the bones of Joseph with him on his journey with the other Israelites.
* Defeating {{E|Ultra Greedier}} as Tainted Forgotten unlocks {{P|XIII - Death?}}, a reversed Major Arcana card associated with longing for an end but not getting it and having to persist without that satisfaction. This could be seen as Isaac not getting an end to his story and having to exist while carrying his bones with him.
* Like all characters that start with only soul/black hearts, Tainted Forgotten's starting health is listed as "-I" on the character selection screen.
* Tainted Forgotten briefly gains flight when he is thrown. This can be noticed if you make a clot with [[Sumptorium]], as the clots will briefly float whenever The Forgotten is thrown.

